                <note rend="inline" type="source">682.00241/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-10T15:00:00-00:44">December 10, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 10—12:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. Legislature passed bill allowing missionaries free entry on personal effects
                    up to $150 yearly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
